From 9473964ab340fc30ead5ad420426ea7d23ac559f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juri Wolf <Amerlander@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 02:18:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Speed up the blocks render server (--docs?render=1)

Every renderblocks job used to recompile the package, fetch semantic.css
and blockly.css again, create and dispose a Blockly workspace, parse the
inlined stylesheet into the svg document and encode a png. A three-block
program took about 1 s per image, so a page rendering many projects (a
class overview) fell far behind.

- compileBlocksAsync keeps the blocks info per package (requests without
  assets) and only re-injects blocks when another render injected others.
- blocklyToSvgAsync fetches the embedded stylesheets once per page and
  splices the css into the serialized svg instead of parsing it into the
  document; the resulting svg is unchanged.
- render() can keep its workspace (reuseWorkspace); the render server
  uses this, so jobs no longer create a workspace and AudioContext each.
- New renderblocks option svgOnly: respond with the svg only, without
  png and base64 data uri. Without it the response is as before.

Measured on twelve sequential jobs of a small program: warm ~1000 ms per
job before, ~340 ms after, ~60 ms with svgOnly. Rendered svgs of the
pxt-calliope blocks tests are identical apart from Blockly's random ids.
---
 pxtblocks/layout.ts | 42 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 pxtblocks/render.ts | 11 +++++++----
 pxtrunner/runner.ts | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
